WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.934
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
Mr. Haqqani--

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.870
Sirajuddin Haqqani,
welcome to the program.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.204
SIRAJUDDIN HAQQANI:
[non-english speech]

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.574
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR: Now,
you have only recently

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.141
shown yourself publicly.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:12.545
Here, it was at a police
passing out parade.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.148
This is your first
proper interview.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.249
Why now?

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.550
SIRAJUDDIN HAQQANI:
[non-english]

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.887
INTERPRETER: Based on
the current necessity,

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:25.425
and because of this necessity,
the local and international

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.194
community had concerns.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.763
Based on the
concerns that existed

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:34.066
on local and
international levels

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:39.272
about a number of individuals
who do not want to be blamed

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:43.108
for implementing
the commitments that

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:47.480
have been made with the
international community.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.981
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
The only thing we really

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:52.318
know about your thoughts
now is something

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:55.655
you wrote for "The New York
Times" back a couple of years

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.590
ago at the beginning
of negotiations

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.592
with the Trump administration.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:02.194
You wrote then that
"I'm confident."

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.663
And you said, "once this
territory is liberated,

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:08.334
we together will find a way
to build an Islamic system

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.836
in which all Afghans
have equal rights, where

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.972
the rights of women that
are granted by Islam,

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:15.541
from the right to education
to the right to work,

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:18.211
are protected, and
where merit is the basis

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:21.280
for equal opportunity."

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:23.616
I want to know whether
you still believe that.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.285
SIRAJUDDIN HAQQANI:
[non-english speech]

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:32.124 line:8%
INTERPRETER: The commitments
that have been made--

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:37.530 line:8%
the situation at the time
was a situation of war.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.632 line:8%
The opposing parties
have provided

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.868 line:8%
a very bad picture
and definition

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:45.805 line:14%
of our administration.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:49.509 line:8%
We wanted to take over the
government by peaceful means.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:53.946 line:8%
And the former government,
with the assistance

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:58.083 line:8%
of some other circles,
sabotaged our particular plan

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:02.321 line:8%
or program, the
transfer of power

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:05.758 line:14%
under military conditions.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:11.397
Currently, there are a large
amount of rumors and hearsay.

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:13.866
And for this reason,
the strong decision

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:21.341
is under way so that we can
implement the commitments that

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:27.280
have been made by us within
an environment of trust

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.383
so that we can implement
those commitments.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.090
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
Many times I

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:41.494
have spoken occasionally
to Taliban leaders,

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.029
even back in the 1990s.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.266
And they told me
something similar,

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.102
that it will take time.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.138
And yet it never happened.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:57.043
Do you believe that young
girls, secondary school

00:02:57.143 --> 00:03:01.214
girls will be allowed to go
to school here in Afghanistan?

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.585
SIRAJUDDIN HAQQANI:
[non-english speech]

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:10.456
INTERPRETER: I would like to
provide some clarification.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:15.160
There is no one who opposes
education for women.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:20.366 line:8%
And already, girls are allowed
to go to school up to grade 6

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.501 line:14%
and above that grade.

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:26.039 line:8%
The work is continuing
on a mechanism.

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:29.909
You may have heard that this
is not opposed at the level

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:32.745
of leadership or the cabinet.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:38.617
But the issue has been
postponed until further notice.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:42.522
In the declaration provided
by the Ministry of Education,

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:46.726
there were some shortcoming
within the preparation

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.961
that were ongoing.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:52.799
Work is ongoing on those issues.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:55.968
Through this interview
and news channel,

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.704
I am assuring that
there is no one

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:02.508
opposed to education,
only that work

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.544
has started on the mechanism.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.716
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
Could you tell us when

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:11.884
you think that will happen?

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:15.054
I know there has been a
big meeting in Kandahar

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:18.357
with your Supreme
Leader Mr. Akhunzada.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.326
Can you tell me whether
any decisions were

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:24.730
made over this past few days?

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.299
SIRAJUDDIN HAQQANI:
[non-english speech]

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.534 line:8%
INTERPRETER: What
I am saying to you

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:31.604 line:8%
is that very soon you
will hear very good news

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:34.740 line:14%
about this issue, God willing.

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:37.009 line:14%
We will specify the time.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:40.847 line:8%
On the arrangement that has
been provided by the leadership,

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.082 line:14%
work is ongoing on that.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:46.085 line:8%
And you will hear
very good news soon.

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:50.956
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
Can I ask you--

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:53.025
I don't know whether
you have any daughters.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:57.297
But do you favor your daughters
going to secondary school?

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:03.569
SIRAJUDDIN HAQQANI:
[non-english speech]

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.638
INTERPRETER: We all believe
that education has been created

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:09.708
as a blessing from
God, which has

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:13.679
been made essential
to both men and women.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:19.051
As I mentioned earlier, there is
no one is opposed to education.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:22.655
The problem is education
based on the Afghan way

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.525
of thinking, and
understanding the culture

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:28.961
aspect of Afghanistan.

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:31.563
There is an issue of
making arrangement

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:35.902
of Islamic rules and principle.

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:38.104 line:8%
On a broader level,
the situation

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:42.541 line:8%
that exists in Afghanistan
concerning the issue of hijab,

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.543 line:8%
because if someone
is giving away

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:50.316 line:8%
their daughters or sisters, they
do that based on total trust.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:54.119 line:8%
We must establish the
conditions so that we can ensure

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.955 line:14%
their honor and security.

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:58.024 line:14%
We are acting to ensure this.

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:05.063
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
I'm going to come

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:06.299
back to this in a minute.

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:08.134
But first, I want to ask
you about the United States

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.202
because many people
in the United States

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:12.404
are obviously interested.

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:15.007
Now, you have signs
and slogans that I've

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:18.511
seen painted on the
walls, some of them

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:21.780
touting defeating
the United States.

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:25.250
Some of them say that you are
by the people, of the people.

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:32.058
About America-- do you consider
America still to be your enemy?

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:42.902
SIRAJUDDIN HAQQANI:
[non-english speech]

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:45.404 line:8%
INTERPRETER: I would like to
make a small clarification.

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:48.574 line:8%
The period of the last
20 years was a situation

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:51.911 line:14%
of defensive fighting and war.

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:53.946 line:8%
When the agreement
was made in Doha,

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:58.517 line:8%
we decided that we would
not be talking about this.

00:06:58.618 --> 00:07:00.652 line:8%
In the future, we
would like to have

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:02.788 line:8%
good relations with
the United States

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:06.358 line:8%
and the international
community based

00:07:06.459 --> 00:07:11.263 line:8%
on rules and principles that
exist in the rest of the world.

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:13.432
And based on that
arrangement, we

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:15.534
have made commitment with them.

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:20.239
And currently, we do not
look at them as enemies.

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:24.477
But based on their conduct,
the Afghans have reservations

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:27.146
about their intentions.

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:31.516
From our side, the freedom
of the country and struggling

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:37.122
for the country's defense is a
legitimate right in accordance

00:07:37.223 --> 00:07:40.526
with the international rules.

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:44.697
Currently, we do not
look at them as enemies.

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:49.502
And we have, time and again,
spoken about diplomacy.

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:52.271
We are committed to
the Doha agreement.

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:55.074 line:8%
Like the rest of the
world, we want relations

00:07:55.174 --> 00:08:00.446 line:8%
with them based on principles
and diplomatic norms

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:03.950 line:8%
that they establish
with us, and that they

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.551 line:14%
don't go back on that.

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:14.726
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
We'll get to some

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.128
of those reasons in a moment.

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:18.731
But I do have to ask you, Mr.
Haqqani, because you know very

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:21.533
well that you are under
personal sanctions

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:24.503
by the United States,
which also has

00:08:24.604 --> 00:08:28.040
a multimillion-dollar
bounty on your head.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:31.643
This is what a top
Western official

00:08:31.744 --> 00:08:34.413
told me just before I got here.

00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:37.083
He said, "We're in a new world.

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:39.118
The guy"-- that's you--

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:42.154
"has a huge amount of
American blood on his hands.

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:44.990
He's got in the
Taliban the tightest

00:08:45.091 --> 00:08:47.193
ties to extremist movements.

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:49.761
He was also one of
the first to put women

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:51.831
back to work in his ministry.

00:08:51.931 --> 00:08:55.334
We have seen his ministry
take promising steps

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:57.436
to contain terrorism.

00:08:57.537 --> 00:09:00.639
To call it a paradox
is an understatement.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:02.307
This is not just my opinion.

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:04.844
It's the opinion of
every single envoy

00:09:04.944 --> 00:09:07.780
who works on these issues."

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:11.550
So on the one hand, they
believe you're a terrorist,

00:09:11.651 --> 00:09:14.553
I'm sorry to say. that's
they who say that.

00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:19.025
On the other hand, they
think they can work with you.

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:20.760
What do you say to that?

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:24.196
SIRAJUDDIN HAQQANI:
[non-english speech]

00:09:24.297 --> 00:09:26.232
INTERPRETER: I would say
that this is a judgment

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:28.534
that they should make.

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:31.002 line:8%
I have mentioned this
before, that they

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:33.672 line:14%
have fought us intensely.

00:09:33.773 --> 00:09:36.942 line:8%
And in order to defend
the country and ourselves,

00:09:37.043 --> 00:09:40.078 line:14%
our response was the same.

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:44.383 line:8%
But the commitment and
the form of governance,

00:09:44.483 --> 00:09:47.185 line:8%
in order to create
secure Afghanistan,

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:51.190 line:8%
we sent a positive
message to the world

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:55.427 line:8%
and sent a positive
message to our nation,

00:09:55.528 --> 00:10:01.033 line:8%
while the previous situation
had concealed our real picture.

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:06.338
And currently, praise God,
under the conditions of freedom,

00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:09.374
our conduct is being
revealed gradually

00:10:09.475 --> 00:10:12.278
to the international community.

00:10:12.378 --> 00:10:16.348
And also, this has been
revealed to certain circles

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:20.453
within the country who are
thinking negatively about us.

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:30.796
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
One of the key pledges

00:10:30.896 --> 00:10:33.598
you made to the United States
was that Afghanistan would

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:36.568
never again be used as
a basis for terrorism

00:10:36.669 --> 00:10:39.104
against the US or its allies.

00:10:39.205 --> 00:10:41.173
Do you-- are you still
committed to that?

00:10:41.273 --> 00:10:44.876
And how do you explain,
in recent months,

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:49.615
there have been attacks here,
people saying that they belong

00:10:49.715 --> 00:10:55.220
to ISIS, ISIS-K, increasingly
bold attacks on, you know,

00:10:55.321 --> 00:10:59.491
on education centers,
even on mosques, on a bus,

00:10:59.592 --> 00:11:00.826
even on a school.

00:11:00.926 --> 00:11:03.362
Some 100 or so people
have been killed

00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:05.498
in recent weeks and months.

00:11:05.598 --> 00:11:10.102
I mean, that doesn't look
like a very secure situation.

00:11:10.202 --> 00:11:11.737
SIRAJUDDIN HAQQANI:
[non-english speech]

00:11:13.606 --> 00:11:16.608 line:8%
INTERPRETER: The commitments
that we have made, if you think

00:11:16.709 --> 00:11:21.780 line:8%
about it, during the 14 months
after Doha, even though there

00:11:21.881 --> 00:11:24.916 line:8%
were a large number of
transgressions continuing

00:11:25.017 --> 00:11:28.120 line:8%
from the opposing
side against us,

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:31.189 line:8%
our leadership was
making recommendations

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:36.695 line:8%
to us repeatedly that we should
stick to our commitment as well

00:11:36.796 --> 00:11:39.731 line:8%
as the fact that until
the liberation of Kabul,

00:11:39.832 --> 00:11:43.502 line:8%
we were making effort
to uphold our commitment

00:11:43.602 --> 00:11:47.005 line:8%
and come to power
through peaceful means.

00:11:47.106 --> 00:11:50.308
Here, we have internal threats.

00:11:50.409 --> 00:11:53.378
And some are deliberately
elevating the threats

00:11:53.479 --> 00:11:58.517
to portray them as a cause
of concern for the nation

00:11:58.617 --> 00:12:01.286
and for the
international community.

00:12:01.387 --> 00:12:04.623
There can be threats to the
rest of the world that are

00:12:04.724 --> 00:12:06.992
orchestrated by a government.

00:12:07.093 --> 00:12:10.829
But we would like to strongly
reassure the rest of the world

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:15.868
that our land will not be
used as a threat to anyone.

